      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems this would try to produce the following when using DirCache:\n\n    1. file: cache/example.org (ecdsa)\n    2. dir: cache/example.org\n    3. file: cache/example.org/rsa\n    4. file: cache/example.org/token\n\nwhere (1) and (2) cannot exist on most filesystems.\nhow about this:\n\n    c.domain + \".rsa\"\n    c.domain + \".token\"\n\nor\n\n    \"rsa/\" + c.domain\n    \"token/\" + c.domain\n\nThe isToken field seems to complicate things though. OTOH I like it being there because I think it might be useful when implementing tls-alpn challenge.",
